            "output": " strtof, strtod, strtold - cppreference.com             \n\n##### [cppreference.com](/)\n\n##### Search\n\n  🔍\n\n[Create account](/index.php?title=Special:CreateAccount&returnto=c%2Fstring%2Fbyte%2Fstrtof \"You are encouraged to create an account and log in; however, it is not mandatory\")\n\n-   [Log in](/index.php?title=Special:UserLogin&returnto=c%2Fstring%2Fbyte%2Fstrtof \"You are encouraged to log in; however, it is not mandatory [o]\")\n\n##### Namespaces\n\n-   [Page](/c/string/byte/strtof \"View the content page [c]\")\n-   [Discussion](/Talk:c/string/byte/strtof \"Discussion about the content page [t]\")\n\n##### Variants[](#)\n\n##### Views\n\n-   [Read](/c/string/byte/strtof)\n-   [View source](/index.php?title=c/string/byte/strtof&action=edit \"This page is protected.\n    You can view its source [e]\")\n-   [View history](/index.php?title=c/string/byte/strtof&action=history \"Past revisions of this page [h]\")\n\n##### Actions[](#)\n\n# strtof, strtod, strtold\n\nFrom cppreference.com\n\n< [c](/c \"c\") | [string](/c/string \"c/string\") | [byte](/c/string/byte \"c/string/byte\")\n\n[C](/c \"c\")\n\n[Compiler support](/c/compiler_support \"c/compiler support\")\n\n[Language](/c/language \"c/language\")\n\n[Headers](/c/header \"c/header\")\n\n[Type support](/c/types \"c/types\")\n\n[Program utilities](/c/program \"c/program\")\n\n[Variadic function support](/c/variadic \"c/variadic\")\n\n[Error handling](/c/error \"c/error\")\n\n[Dynamic memory management](/c/memory \"c/memory\")\n\n[Strings library](/c/string \"c/string\")\n\n[Algorithms](/c/algorithm \"c/algorithm\")\n\n[Numerics](/c/numeric \"c/numeric\")\n\n[Date and time utilities](/c/chrono \"c/chrono\")\n\n[Input/output support](/c/io \"c/io\")\n\n[Localization support](/c/locale \"c/locale\")\n\n[Concurrency support](/c/thread \"c/thread\") (C11)\n\n[Technical Specifications](/c/experimental \"c/experimental\")\n\n[Symbol index](/c/symbol_index \"c/symbol index\")\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:c/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n[Strings library](/c/string \"c/string\")\n\n[Null-terminated byte strings](/c/string/byte \"c/string/byte\")\n\n[Null-terminated multibyte strings](/c/string/multibyte \"c/string/multibyte\")\n\n[Null-terminated wide strings](/c/string/wide \"c/string/wide\")\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:c/string/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n[Null-terminated byte strings](/c/string/byte \"c/string/byte\")\n\nFunctions\n\nCharacter manipulation\n\n[isalnum](/c/string/byte/isalnum \"c/string/byte/isalnum\")\n\n[isalpha](/c/string/byte/isalpha \"c/string/byte/isalpha\")\n\n[islower](/c/string/byte/islower \"c/string/byte/islower\")\n\n[isupper](/c/string/byte/isupper \"c/string/byte/isupper\")\n\n[isdigit](/c/string/byte/isdigit \"c/string/byte/isdigit\")\n\n[isxdigit](/c/string/byte/isxdigit \"c/string/byte/isxdigit\")\n\n[isblank](/c/string/byte/isblank \"c/string/byte/isblank\")\n\n(C99)\n\n[iscntrl](/c/string/byte/iscntrl \"c/string/byte/iscntrl\")\n\n[isgraph](/c/string/byte/isgraph \"c/string/byte/isgraph\")\n\n[isspace](/c/string/byte/isspace \"c/string/byte/isspace\")\n\n[isprint](/c/string/byte/isprint \"c/string/byte/isprint\")\n\n[ispunct](/c/string/byte/ispunct \"c/string/byte/ispunct\")\n\n[tolower](/c/string/byte/tolower \"c/string/byte/tolower\")\n\n[toupper](/c/string/byte/toupper \"c/string/byte/toupper\")\n\nConversions to and from numeric formats\n\n[atoiatolatoll](/c/string/byte/atoi \"c/string/byte/atoi\")\n\n(C99)\n\n[atof](/c/string/byte/atof \"c/string/byte/atof\")\n\n[strtolstrtoll](/c/string/byte/strtol \"c/string/byte/strtol\")\n\n(C99)\n\n[strtoulstrtoull](/c/string/byte/strtoul \"c/string/byte/strtoul\")\n\n(C99)\n\n[strtoimaxstrtoumax](/c/string/byte/strtoimax \"c/string/byte/strtoimax\")\n\n(C99)(C99)\n\nstrtofstrtodstrtold\n\n(C99)(C99)\n\n[strfromfstrfromdstrfroml](/c/string/byte/strfromf \"c/string/byte/strfromf\")\n\n(C23)(C23)(C23)\n\nString manipulation\n\n[strcpystrcpy\\_s](/c/string/byte/strcpy \"c/string/byte/strcpy\")\n\n(C11)\n\n[strncpystrncpy\\_s](/c/string/byte/strncpy \"c/string/byte/strncpy\")\n\n(C11)\n\n[strcatstrcat\\_s](/c/string/byte/strcat \"c/string/byte/strcat\")\n\n(C11)\n\n[strncatstrncat\\_s](/c/string/byte/strncat \"c/string/byte/strncat\")\n\n(C11)\n\n[strxfrm](/c/string/byte/strxfrm \"c/string/byte/strxfrm\")\n\n[strdup](/c/string/byte/strdup \"c/string/byte/strdup\")\n\n(C23)\n\n[strndup](/c/string/byte/strndup \"c/string/byte/strndup\")\n\n(C23)\n\n  \n\nString examination\n\n[strlenstrnlen\\_s](/c/string/byte/strlen \"c/string/byte/strlen\")\n\n(C11)\n\n[strcmp](/c/string/byte/strcmp \"c/string/byte/strcmp\")\n\n[strncmp](/c/string/byte/strncmp \"c/string/byte/strncmp\")\n\n[strcoll](/c/string/byte/strcoll \"c/string/byte/strcoll\")\n\n[strchr](/c/string/byte/strchr \"c/string/byte/strchr\")\n\n[strrchr](/c/string/byte/strrchr \"c/string/byte/strrchr\")\n\n[strspn](/c/string/byte/strspn \"c/string/byte/strspn\")\n\n[strcspn](/c/string/byte/strcspn \"c/string/byte/strcspn\")\n\n[strpbrk](/c/string/byte/strpbrk \"c/string/byte/strpbrk\")\n\n[strstr](/c/string/byte/strstr \"c/string/byte/strstr\")\n\n[strtokstrtok\\_s](/c/string/byte/strtok \"c/string/byte/strtok\")\n\n(C11)\n\n  \n\nMemory manipulation\n\n[memchr](/c/string/byte/memchr \"c/string/byte/memchr\")\n\n[memcmp](/c/string/byte/memcmp \"c/string/byte/memcmp\")\n\n[memsetmemset\\_explicitmemset\\_s](/c/string/byte/memset \"c/string/byte/memset\")\n\n(C23)(C11)\n\n[memcpymemcpy\\_s](/c/string/byte/memcpy \"c/string/byte/memcpy\")\n\n(C11)\n\n[memmovememmove\\_s](/c/string/byte/memmove \"c/string/byte/memmove\")\n\n(C11)\n\n[memccpy](/c/string/byte/memccpy \"c/string/byte/memccpy\")\n\n(C23)\n\nMiscellaneous\n\n[strerrorstrerror\\_sstrerrorlen\\_s](/c/string/byte/strerror \"c/string/byte/strerror\")\n\n(C11)(C11)\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:c/string/byte/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\nDefined in header `[<stdlib.h>](/c/header/stdlib \"c/header/stdlib\")`\n\nfloat       strtof ( const char\\* restrict str, char\\*\\* restrict str\\_end );\n\n(1)\n\n(since C99)\n\ndouble      strtod ( const char\\*          str, char\\*\\*          str\\_end );\n\n(2)\n\n(until C99)\n\ndouble      strtod ( const char\\* restrict str, char\\*\\* restrict str\\_end );\n\n(since C99)\n\nlong double strtold( const char\\* restrict str, char\\*\\* restrict str\\_end );\n\n(3)\n\n(since C99)\n\nInterprets a floating-point value in a byte string pointed to by `str`.\n\nFunction discards any whitespace characters (as determined by [isspace](/c/string/byte/isspace \"c/string/byte/isspace\")) until first non-whitespace character is found. Then it takes as many characters as possible to form a valid floating-point representation and converts them to a floating-point value. The valid floating-point value can be one of the following:\n\n-   decimal floating-point expression. It consists of the following parts:\n\n-   (optional) plus or minus sign\n-   nonempty sequence of decimal digits optionally containing decimal-point character (as determined by the current C [locale](/c/locale/setlocale \"c/locale/setlocale\")) (defines significand)\n-   (optional) `**e**` or `**E**` followed with optional minus or plus sign and nonempty sequence of decimal digits (defines exponent to base 10)\n\n-   hexadecimal floating-point expression. It consists of the following parts:\n\n-   (optional) plus or minus sign\n-   `**0x**` or `**0X**`\n-   nonempty sequence of hexadecimal digits optionally containing a decimal-point character (as determined by the current C [locale](/c/locale/setlocale \"c/locale/setlocale\")) (defines significand)\n-   (optional) `**p**` or `**P**` followed with optional minus or plus sign and nonempty sequence of decimal digits (defines exponent to base 2)\n\n-   infinity expression. It consists of the following parts:\n\n-   (optional) plus or minus sign\n-   `**INF**` or `**INFINITY**` ignoring case\n\n-   not-a-number expression. It consists of the following parts:\n\n-   (optional) plus or minus sign\n-   `**NAN**` or `**NAN(**`*char\\_sequence* ﻿`**)**` ignoring case of the `**NAN**` part. *char\\_sequence* can only contain digits, Latin letters, and underscores. The result is a quiet NaN floating-point value.\n\n(since C99)\n\n-   any other expression that may be accepted by the currently installed C [locale](/c/locale/setlocale \"c/locale/setlocale\").\n\nThe functions sets the pointer pointed to by `str_end` to point to the character past the last character interpreted. If `str_end` is a null pointer, it is ignored.\n\n## Contents\n\n-   [1 Parameters](#Parameters)\n-   [2 Return value](#Return_value)\n-   [3 Example](#Example)\n-   [4 References](#References)\n-   [5 See also](#See_also)\n\n### Parameters\n\nstr\n\n\\-\n\npointer to the null-terminated byte string to be interpreted\n\nstr\\_end\n\n\\-\n\npointer to a pointer to character\n\n### Return value\n\nFloating-point value corresponding to the contents of `str` on success. If the converted value falls out of range of corresponding return type, range error occurs ([errno](/c/error/errno \"c/error/errno\") is set to [ERANGE](/c/error/errno_macros \"c/error/errno macros\")) and [HUGE\\_VAL](/c/numeric/math/HUGE_VAL \"c/numeric/math/HUGE VAL\"), [HUGE\\_VALF](/c/numeric/math/HUGE_VAL \"c/numeric/math/HUGE VAL\") or [HUGE\\_VALL](/c/numeric/math/HUGE_VAL \"c/numeric/math/HUGE VAL\") is returned. If no conversion can be performed, `0` is returned.\n\n### Example\n\nRun this code\n\n#include <errno.h>\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n\nint main(void)\n{\n    // parsing with error handling\n    const char\\* p \\= \"111.11 -2.22 Nan nan(2) inF 0X1.BC70A3D70A3D7P+6  1.18973e+4932zzz\";\n    printf(\"Parsing '%s':\\\\n\", p);\n    char\\* end \\= NULL;\n    for (double f \\= strtod(p, &end); p != end; f \\= strtod(p, &end))\n    {\n        printf(\"'%.\\*s' -> \", (int)(end \\- p), p);\n        p \\= end;\n        if (errno \\== ERANGE)\n        {\n            printf(\"range error, got \");\n            errno \\= 0;\n        }\n        printf(\"%f\\\\n\", f);\n    }\n\n    // parsing without error handling\n    printf(\"\\\\\"  -0.0000000123junk\\\\\"  -->  %g\\\\n\", strtod(\"  -0.0000000123junk\", NULL));\n    printf(\"\\\\\"junk\\\\\"                 -->  %g\\\\n\", strtod(\"junk\", NULL));\n}\n\nPossible output:\n\nParsing '111.11 -2.22 Nan nan(2) inF 0X1.BC70A3D70A3D7P+6  1.18973e+4932zzz':\n'111.11' -> 111.110000\n' -2.22' -> -2.220000\n' Nan' -> nan\n' nan(2)' -> nan\n' inF' -> inf\n' 0X1.BC70A3D70A3D7P+6' -> 111.110000\n'  1.18973e+4932' -> range error, got inf\n\"  -0.0000000123junk\"  -->  -1.23e-08\n\"junk\"                 -->  0\n\n### References\n\n-   C23 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2024):\n\n-   7.22.1.3 The strtod, strtof, and strtold functions (p: TBD)\n\n-   C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018):\n\n-   7.22.1.3 The strtod, strtof, and strtold functions (p: 249-251)\n\n-   C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011):\n\n-   7.22.1.3 The strtod, strtof, and strtold functions (p: 342-344)\n\n-   C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999):\n\n-   7.20.1.3 The strtod, strtof, and strtold functions (p: 308-310)\n\n-   C89/C90 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1990):\n\n-   4.10.1.4 The strtod function\n\n### See also\n\n[atof](/c/string/byte/atof \"c/string/byte/atof\")\n\nconverts a byte string to a floating-point value  \n(function) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:c/string/byte/dsc_atof&action=edit)\n\n[wcstofwcstodwcstold](/c/string/wide/wcstof \"c/string/wide/wcstof\")\n\n(C99)(C95)(C99)\n\nconverts a wide string to a floating-point value  \n(function) [\\[edit\\]](https://cppreference.com/index.php?title=Template:c/string/wide/dsc_wcstof&action=edit)\n\n[C++ documentation](/cpp/string/byte/strtof \"cpp/string/byte/strtof\") for strtof, strtod, strtold\n\n[Categories](/Special:Categories \"Special:Categories\"):\n\n-   [Pages using deprecated source tags](/index.php?title=Category:Pages_using_deprecated_source_tags&action=edit&redlink=1 \"Category:Pages using deprecated source tags (page does not exist)\")\n-   [Pages using deprecated enclose attributes](/index.php?title=Category:Pages_using_deprecated_enclose_attributes&action=edit&redlink=1 \"Category:Pages using deprecated enclose attributes (page does not exist)\")\n\n##### Navigation\n\n-   [Support us](http://www.cppreference.com/support)\n-   [Recent changes](/Special:RecentChanges \"A list of recent changes in the wiki [r]\")\n-   [FAQ](/Cppreference:FAQ)\n-   [Offline version](/Cppreference:Archives)\n\n##### Tools[](#)\n\n-   [What links here](/Special:WhatLinksHere/c/string/byte/strtof \"A list of all wiki pages that link here [j]\")\n-   [Related changes](/Special:RecentChangesLinked/c/string/byte/strtof \"Recent changes in pages linked from this page [k]\")\n-   [Upload file](http://upload.cppreference.com/w/Special:Upload \"Upload files [u]\")\n-   [Special pages](/Special:SpecialPages \"A list of all special pages [q]\")\n-   [Printable version](javascript:print\\(\\); \"Printable version of this page [p]\")\n-   [Permanent link](/index.php?title=c/string/byte/strtof&oldid=178833 \"Permanent link to this revision of this page\")\n-   [Page information](/index.php?title=c/string/byte/strtof&action=info \"More information about this page\")\n\n-   In other languages\n\n-   [العربية](http://ar.cppreference.com/c/string/byte/strtof \"c/string/byte/strtof – العربية\")\n-   [Čeština](https://cs.cppreference.com/c/string/byte/strtof \"c/string/byte/strtof – čeština\")\n-   [Deutsch](https://de.cppreference.com/c/string/byte/strtof \"c/string/byte/strtof – Deutsch\")\n-   [Español](http://es.cppreference.com/c/string/byte/strtof \"c/string/byte/strtof – español\")\n-   [Français](http://fr.cppreference.com/c/string/byte/strtof \"c/string/byte/strtof – français\")\n-   [Italiano](http://it.cppreferenc