cts the note at 2032. So another table/note inconsistency. Need to fix.\n\nSo for point 1: Their PROSE notes (2031-2045) are accurate and well-stated. But:\n(a) the TABLE rows (2002, 2006) still contain the old claims that the run disproved → contradiction.\n(b) line 2036 states the fact but doesn't say it contradicts the standard (loses the \"aha\").\n(c) minor: could add concrete examples for hex token set.\n(d) They didn't record that the `scientific`/`fixed` exponent rules were confirmed (line 2039 says \"как описано на cppref\" — that's fine, it's confirmation).\n(e) They didn't note the `%a` formatting quirk (MSVC `1.5p+5` без 0x) — relevant for comparing with GCC next. Worth adding so they don't misread VM output. This is useful for point 2!\n(f) Line 2018-2020 (old hypothesis about underflow) now superseded by 2035; could mark as resolved or leave (it's a historical note). Fine.\n(g) Line 2051 says \"пока ничто из этого не проверено\" — but it IS now checked (2035). Stale statement under \"Что заметила при работе с deepseek\". Hmm — line 2051 is in the \"что заметила\" section and says the hypotheses are unverified. Now they're verified (partially). So stale. Should update or add a pointer.\n\nActually careful: line 2051 says the hypothesis about strtod giving 0 for underflow is unverified. Now verified: for 1e-400, strtod → 0.0 + ERANGE. For 1e-320 → subnormal (so \"воспринято как нуль\" is not universal — confirms my earlier point). So the journal should reflect: hypothesis partially confirmed (gross underflow → 0; near boundary → subnormal). Line 2051 stale.\n\n(h) Open items list (2056-2059): now that MSVC run is done, items 0x-prefix and p/P and underflow are closed for MSVC, but GCC remains. The list should be updated to \"remaining for GCC: 0x at general; value-on-out_of_range; ...\". Actually item 2059's underflow is now answered for MSVC. Should mark.\n\n(i) `parse_diff.cpp` code itself isn't in the journal (only the case list). Fine.\n\nSo my answer to point 1: The observations in 2031-2045 are accurate — I cross-checked each against the run. But there are stale contradictions: the table rows 2002/2006 still assert what the run disproved; line 2036 should name the standard (MSVC deviates, not just \"MSVC does X\"); line 2051 still says \"не проверено\"; the open-items list 2056-2059 needs updating (MSVC done). Plus add the `%a` quirk.\n\nLet me be precise and list these.\n\nActually, wait — I should double check the exact current text of rows 2002 and 2006. Let me read 1997-2008. The grep showed mojibake but line 2002 still the hex row with \"также воспринимает\", and 2006/2007 with \"value остаётся нетронутым\". Let me read to be sure of exact wording.\n\nLet me read offset 1997 limit 12.\n\nActually I have earlier reads: line 2002 (from the 2050-line version) was: \"| hex-число | воспринимает 0x, 0X | также воспринимает, но если bitmask `std::chars_format::hex`, то при 0х/0Х в начале распознавание остановится на \"х\" и распознается только нуль. т.к. с этой бит-маской и так ожидается 16ричное число|\". And in the 2055-line version, line 2002 had that. And the latest (2078) grep shows line 2002 similar. Good.\n\nAnd line 2006: \"...value остаётся нетронутым\". Good.\n\nSo no need to re-read; but let me be safe and read 1997-2010 quickly. Actually I already have enough. But to quote exactly in my corrections, I'll read.\n\nHmm, plan mode allows reads. Let me just do one read of 1997-2010 to be precise. Actually the previous read (2055 version) gave lines 1997-2008 exactly. The line numbers shifted (removed \"что распознаёт\" row). Let me map: In the 2055 version I read, line 1999 was \"знак плюс\"... In the 2078 version, the grep shows line 2002 = hex row, 2006 = \"что возвращает при выходе...\", 2007 = \"что возвращает если не может...\". So rows shifted +2. So:\n- hex row = 2002\n- что возвращает при выходе за диапазон = 2006\n- что возвращает если не может сконвертировать = 2007\n\nOK. I'll quote approximately, or read to be exact. Let me read 1997-2008 to be precise since I'm making corrections.\n\nActually, I'll just read it. One quick read.\n\nThen compose the answer:\n\nPart 1: verification of their notes.\n- Prose 2031-2045: accurate, cross-checked each bullet.\n- But: contradictions with table (2002, 2006) — stale.\n- 2036 missing the standard reference → doesn't show it's a deviation.\n- 2051 stale (\"не проверено\").\n- 2056-2059 open items stale (MSVC closed, GCC remains).\n- Add `%a` quirk (important for part 2).\n- Add concrete hex examples optional.\n\nPart 2: GCC command.\n- `cl` → `g++`. `-oparse_diff` works attached but clearer `-o parse_diff`. Need to name the source and run it.\n- Full: `g++ -std=c++23 -Wall -Wextra parse_diff.cpp -o parse_diff && ./parse_diff > parse_diff_gcc.txt`\n- Check `g++ --version` ≥13 (std::format needs GCC 13+; and `std::expected` 12+; `std::print` 14+ but not used). If GCC 12 → std::format unavailable → fallback needed.\n- Note: copy the ASCII .cpp from Windows (encoding not an issue since ASCII).\n- Note: `%a` output differs (GCC prints 0x...), so don't misread.\n- Also `-o` attached form: `-oparse_diff` is accepted by GCC (option arg can be attached), so not a fatal mistake, but `cl` is.\n\nWait, is `-oparse_diff` really accepted? GCC's option parsing: options that take an argument accept both `-o file` and `-ofile`. E.g. `gcc -ohello hello.c` works. Yes, I'm fairly confident. I'll say \"`-oparse_diff` GCC поймёт (присоединённый аргумент), но `cl` — нет\".\n\nAlso: they might also need `-lstdc++`? No.\n\nAlso: to compare outputs fairly, use same flags. And note MSVC output had `errno=ERANGE` etc.\n\nAlso: maybe compile with `-fsanitize=address`? Not needed.\n\nAlso: `g++` on Ubuntu might be `g++-13`. `g++ --version` first.\n\nLet me also mention: since the program uses `std::format`, on Ubuntu if libstdc++ < 13 the compile fails; the error would be about `<format>`. Then fallback to printf version (I can provide).\n\nNow